<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antonio de Ulloa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1716">1716</a>–<a href="/years/1795">1795</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antonio de Ulloa (1716–1795) was a Spanish naval officer and scientist who took part in the French geodesic mission to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> from 1735, and whose account of the voyage first described platinum to European science. Appointed the first Spanish governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louisiana">Louisiana</a>, he arrived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a> in 1766, but his weak forces and trade restrictions provoked the Louisiana Rebellion of 1768, which expelled him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antonio-de-ulloa.jpg" alt="Antonio de Ulloa" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Andrés Cortés y Aguilar · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Almirante_Antonio_de_Ulloa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
